## Skills Protocol (MUST FOLLOW)

**Standing rules:**
- **Silent skipping = failure mode.** If you catch yourself improvising what looks like a skill's job (your own consistency check, your own verification routine), STOP and fire the skill instead.
- **User phrasing matching a skill name IS the trigger.** *"run a consistency check"* / *"brainstorm this"* / *"verify it"* / *"design review"* / *"code review"* — those are skill names, not generic verbs.

### The 8 🔒 MUST-USE skills (auto-fire on trigger match, no permission ask)

| Skill | Trigger |
|---|---|
| `using-superpowers` | Always, at chat start. |
| `brainstorming` | Before ANY creative work — new feature, mechanic, UI, or behaviour change. |
| `test-driven-development` | Before writing implementation code. |
| `systematic-debugging` | IMMEDIATELY on any bug / hang / crash / wrong-output report, OR before asking someone to run a manual test. Phase 1 evidence-gathering FIRST — no fix attempts before that. |
| `verification-before-completion` | Before ANY "done / fixed / passing" claim, before commits, before PRs. Run actual verification commands; cite the output. |
| `{{ENGINE}} skill` | When editing engine files (scripts, scenes, resources, shaders), creating an autoload/scene, or authoring a spec that will produce such files. <!-- e.g. anthropic-skills:godot, anthropic-skills:unity-development --> |
| `session-close` | On ANY session-end signal ("wrap up", "we're done", "close session"), OR after 5+ commits without a sync. MUST fire before the session ends. |
| `writing-skills` | Before editing or creating any `SKILL.md` file. Self-check before any Write/Edit on a SKILL.md path: did `writing-skills` fire this turn? If not, fire it FIRST. |

**Failure-mode enforcement:** claiming done without `verification-before-completion`, proposing a fix without `systematic-debugging` Phase 1, or touching an engine file without the `{{ENGINE}}` skill primed are all protocol violations. Push back on them.

