## MANDATORY DISPATCH rule

**Before any non-trivial scoped work, check `docs/agents-index.md` Intent → Agent table. If the work maps to a specialist's domain, propose dispatching that specialist FIRST.** Doing it inline when an agent should own it is the same failure mode as silent skill skipping.

**Self-check before non-trivial work:**
1. Match the request against the Intent → Agent table.
2. If a specialist owns it: announce *"This is `<agent>` territory — propose dispatching."* and wait.
3. Inline is OK only if (a) trivial (small doc tweak, <~50 LOC), OR (b) the designer explicitly says "do it yourself."

Rationalizations that do NOT excuse skipping dispatch: token cost, "faster inline", "not THAT scoped", "I'll dispatch next time." Dispatch.

