## Pipeline (when to use which path)

Two legitimate paths. The small path is a SUBSET of the large path — it skips the GDD/architecture/epic ceremony. **Default: brainstorm first, THEN choose the path** based on how big the scope turns out to be.

### Small path (single-system work, 1–2 weeks)

```
brainstorming → architecture-decision (ADR) → writing-plans → executing-plans
```
(+ TDD + verification + ship). Optimal when the work fits one ADR with a few batched decisions.

### Large path (multi-vertical, multi-week)

```
brainstorming → design-system (GDD) → map-systems (decompose)
  → create-architecture → create-control-manifest
  → create-epics → create-stories → dev-story
  → qa-plan → test-driven-development → gate-check
  → finishing-a-development-branch
```
Director gates apply between phases. Needed for large, cross-cutting feature areas.

